Mechanisms of cancer initiation
❖ Pathophysiological mechanism of cancer:
考
❑ Genes (proto-oncogenes vs tumor-suppressor genes):
▪ Proto-oncogenes 原癌基因 → Oncogenes 癌基因;
▪ Cannot be simply removed (they are essential genes);
▪ Transformation:
• Increase expression level;
• Increase stability and/or activity;
• Loss of regulation.
▪ Examples:
• Growth factors and their receptors (e.g., EGF, EGFR);
• Tyrosine kinases (e.g., Bcr-Abl);
• Serine/threonine kinases (e.g., cyclin-dependent kinases);
• Regulatory GTPases (e.g., Ras);
• Transcription regulators (e.g., Myc, YAP);
• Others (e.g., Bcl-2).

Mechanisms of cancer initiation
❖ Pathophysiological mechanism of cancer:
考
❑ Genes (proto-oncogenes vs tumor-suppressor genes):
▪ Tumor-suppressor genes 抑癌基因 (TSGs);
▪ Loss of TSGs > activation of oncogenes;
▪ Mutations may occur in non-coding regions and coding regions;
▪ Examples:
• Receptors or signal transducers
for signals that inhibit cell
proliferation (e.g., TGF-β);
• Control cell cycle-specific gene
expression (e.g., pRB);
• Checkpoint-control proteins
(e.g., Brca1);
• Proteins that induce apoptosis
and DNA repairing (e.g., p53);
