Mechanisms of cancer progression
❖ Progression is the late stages of cancer, always happens with
考
metastasis (转移);
❖ Metastasis is the spread of cancer to other locations in the body;
❖ Metastasis can occur via the blood or the lymphatic system or both;
❖ The dispersed tumors are called metastatic tumors (转移瘤), while the
original is called the primary tumor (原位瘤);
❖ Almost all cancers can metastasize;
❖ Most deaths of patients due to
cancer that has metastasized;
❖ Different types of cancers tend
to metastasize to particular
organs. Overall, the most
common places for metastases
to occur are the lung, liver,
brain, and bone.
Credit @ BioRender

Mechanisms of cancer progression
❖ The typical steps in metastasis are:
考
1. Local invasion (侵袭);
2. Intravasation into the blood or lymph;
3. Circulation through the body;
4. Extravasation into the new tissue;
5. Proliferation;
6. Angiogenesis (血管生成).
