Classification of classic cytotoxic drugs
❖ Classification by mechanism of actions (MOAs):
考
❑ Antimetabolites (抗代谢药物) interfere biosynthesis of
nucleic acid;
❑ Alkylating agents (烷化剂) bind and destroy DNA;
❑ Topoisomerase inhibitors (拓扑异构酶抑制剂) inhibit DNA
replication and transcription;
❑ Antimicrotubule agents (抗微管药物) block cell division;
❑ *Anticancer antibiotics (抗癌抗生素).
Front. Oncol., 2022, 12

Alkylating agents
❖ Classical alkylating agents have true alkyl groups:
❑ Nitrogen mustards (氮芥类): e.g., Mechlorethamine (氮芥),
Cyclophosphamide (环磷酰胺);
❑ Nitrosoureas (亚硝基脲类): e.g., Carmustine (卡莫司汀);
❑ Aziridines (环乙亚胺类): e.g., Thiotepa (噻替哌);
❑ Alkyl sulfonates (烷基磺酸类): e.g., Busulfan (白消安);
