Targeted therapy
❖ Targeted therapy, or molecularly-targeted therapy, is one of the major
modalities of medical treatment of cancer.
❖ Targeted therapy interferes specific targeted proteins needed for
carcinogenesis and tumor growth, rather than by simply interfering with all
rapidly dividing cells (e.g. classic cytotoxic drugs).
❖ Biomarkers are usually required to aid the selection of patients who will
likely respond to a given targeted therapy.
❖ Types:
❑ Small molecule drugs vs monoclonal antibodies;
❑ Targets:
▪ Tyrosine kinase;
▪ Serine/threonine kinase;
▪ Cell surface receptors;
▪ Apoptosis factors;
▪ Others……

