blood cells and the epithelium in mouth, stomach, and intestines.
❑ Immunosuppression and myelosuppression;
❑ Gastrointestinal distress;
❑ Anemia;
❑ Nausea and vomiting;
❑ Hair loss;
❑ Infertility;
❑ Teratogenicity;
❑ Cognitive impairment;
❑ Organ damage;
